<title>SOUTH AFRICA: South African clothing industry hard hit by strike.</title>
<headline>South African clothing industry hard hit by strike.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Western Cape clothing industry was hard hit by a 24-strike called by the Congress of South African Trade Unions on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;There are patches where the attendance is normal to good but on the whole absenteeism is about 60 to 70 percent, which is crippling,&quot; Cape Clothing Manufacturers' Association chairman Johann Baard told Reuters.</p>
<p>He said that compared to previous stay-aways, the turn out was &quot;about average&quot;.</p>
<p>Baard said he had heard that the stay-away in KwaZulu-Natal and Gauteng clothing industries was between 80 and 90 percent.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
</text>
